ed by a woman  because it really goes there it does not  hold back it's singular in its tone but  at the same time has a lot to say to  women particularly about anxiety over  your first pregnancy prepartum  depression I think a lot of women will  be able to relate to this it's a really  fun time at the cinema and has a lot to  say  so check out pre venge in select  theaters this weekend so these guys are  really spoiled like mummy I want a  Playstation mummy I want you to kill  that man  [Applause]  and on video-on-demand this week you  have to check out one of my favorite  films from 2016 this is the perfect  movie to watch in the comfort of your  own home it's called Patterson it stars  Adam driver as a bus driver named  Patterson who is living in Paterson New  Jersey it's directed by Jim Jarmusch and  it's all about those little coincidences  those little patterns and the beauty in  day-to-day life it just follows a week  in his life and nothing super dramatic  happens but it's so beautiful it's  absolutely moving and I love the poetry  in it so much so that one of my good  friends Matt actually bought me this  edition of the collected earlier poems  of William Carlos Williams this is the  same edition of a book that Adam drivers  character reads and in one of these  poems is in here and I loved it so much  I knock off work have a beer at the bar  I look down at the glass  and feel glad it's like a gorgeous  meditation on life  check out Patterson on video on demand  including Fandango now from March 21 a  bar survey in Patterson what is very  poetic  so to recap in theaters see Wilson or  pre venge and at home watch Patterson  all those films are well worth your time  well worth your money and indie films of  course always need your support let me  know what you think on Twitter at Alicia  Malone or in the comments below and I'll  see you again next week  [Music]

